# Site security (lean)

Project equivalent of Marketplace `security-guidance` — Cursor-native, no Claude Python hooks.

## Trust boundaries

- Never commit or read `.dev.vars`, `.env*`, PEM/keys (hook already blocks).
- `functions/` is the only server trust boundary: validate all request input; no secrets in responses or client JS.
- Prefer Cloudflare bindings / Dashboard secrets over hardcoding tokens.

## XSS / DOM

- Avoid `innerHTML` / `document.write` with untrusted or URL-derived strings; use `textContent` or safe templates.
- Sanitize any HTML injected into language pages; keep user-facing copy static where possible.

## Shell / Node in tools

- Prefer `execFile` / argv arrays over `exec`/`execSync` with interpolated strings.
- Do not pass untrusted path segments into filesystem or shell commands.

## Review

- On security-sensitive diffs: Cursor **security-review** subagent (`/review-security`) or ask explicitly.
- Do **not** install Marketplace `security-guidance` (Claude-only Stop/commit hooks).